-- title:
--   At a crossing: p a non-zero-divisor, stalk dimension ≥ 2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 1$ together with a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, that every unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$ lies in $H$, and that the $q$-expansion `jqModC` of $j$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field of level $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the bundle of Deligne–Rapoport-type data and properties for the model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over $R_p$ (properness, flatness, integrality and local finite presentation of the structure map, integral closedness of the sections over affine opens, properness and relative smoothness of dimension $1$ at the auxiliary level `ΓN`, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the generic base change and compatible with the Galois action and with $q$-expansions, smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, and the remaining conditions of that structure). Let $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a valuation subring with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ satisfy that $\rho$ followed by the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O : R_p \to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ be a ring map with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ equal to $\rho$ followed by the residue map of $A$. Write $X_O =$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` for the fibre product of the model with $\operatorname{Spec} O$ over $R_p$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two components `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` of the geometric special fibre at $A$, and let $x_n =$ `crossingPt … n` be its image in $X_O$ under the first projection followed by the component map and the base-change comparison map. Assume both `𝔛.ξinf` and `𝔛.ξzero` specialise to $x_n$. Then the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of $X_O$ obtained from $p \in O$ along the structure map to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ is a non-zero-divisor in the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X_O, x_n}$, and the Krull dimension of that stalk is at least $2$ in $\mathbb{N}_\infty \cup \{\bot\}$.
--
--   This is the local algebra at a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$: the uniformiser remains a non-zero-divisor in the local ring, and the local ring has dimension at least two, so the crossing is not a generic point of the special fibre. It is used in the construction of oriented étale charts at crossings (`forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart`), and relies on the integrality of $X_O$ (`isIntegral_xO`) together with the incomparability of the two branch ideals at the crossing (`not_branchIdeal_le_branchIdeal_crossingPt`).
